commit 71bf9a219f390f89cc624f5df30d1d1ae614d949

C03: known-folder listings can be ordered by date and bounded by a requested count (FILES1433, BUILD1433)

H0453 «Cuenta los archivos en el escritorio y lista los 5 mas recientes» had no reader: the known-folder listing (FILES1427) accepted neither an order nor a requested count, and the resolver took «5» as a note cardinality and returned nothing.

Baxy.Kernel ProductCatalog: filesystem.known.list takes an optional order ∈ name/recent.
Baxy.Providers.Windows WindowsKnownFileAdapter.List: order=recent sorts by modification date, newest first, before the limit; the receipt records the order.
baxy_mind effect_intent: _known_folder_recent_listing reads «cuenta los archivos de <carpeta> y lista los N más recientes» and «listá los N archivos más recientes de <carpeta>» (folder, N ≤ 20) and resolve_explicit_effects resolves it before the note-cardinality gate; __main__ grounds folder, order=recent and limit=N; llm projects newestFirst and instructs that the names go from newest to oldest.

Offline probe: the literal and four variants resolve with the right folder and count; a prohibition, a mismatched folder pair and a note request do not; the product compiles and the core advertises the new schema. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


